recommend check-in (either) -- %326 is booked and its repair is proven both ways on the bytes that caused it, with 65 rooms brought inside a guard that saw 17. What stops is the seam the repair cannot reach: claim_preserve is opt-in, so nothing obliges a path-moving commit to run it, and binding the two is a seat rather than a lap. Three items sit with the peer and I touched none -- the foundations_link red from their tools/equinox fold, the card's stale Git nib, and the zero-byte 142844 log. One sits with Keaton: whether constel/LADDER.md's declared Field setting should become Meter, measured F at 56 under Field and A+ at 98 under Meter.
